  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "Out of the countries that the World Bank recorded as having women and girls as less than 45% of their population in 2000, which country had women and girls as the highest average percentage of its population from 2020 through the end of 2023?",
  "answer": "Now I have all the data. Let me calculate the averages and provide the answer.\n\n**Calculation of 2020-2023 averages:**\n\n| Country | 2020 | 2021 | 2022 | 2023 | **Average** |\n|---------|------|------|------|------|-------------|\n| United Arab Emirates | 35.62 | 35.78 | 35.90 | 35.99 | **35.82%** |\n| Qatar | 27.89 | 28.18 | 28.15 | 28.48 | **28.18%** |\n| Bahrain | 37.69 | 38.00 | 38.03 | 37.92 | **37.91%** |\n| **Kuwait** | 39.06 | 39.34 | 38.95 | 38.84 | **39.05%** |\n| Oman | 37.89 | 38.87 | 38.44 | 37.92 | **38.28%** |\n\n**Answer: Kuwait** had the highest average percentage of women and girls (39.05%) from 2020 through 2023 among the five countries that had women/girls below 45% of their population in 2000 (per World Bank indicator SP.POP.TOTL.FE.ZS).\n\n## Sources\n1. World Bank API - Countries with female population <45% in 2000: https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL.FE.ZS?date=2000&format=json&per_page=300\n2. World Bank API - Female population % for 2020-2023: https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/ARE;QAT;BHR;KWT;OMN/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL.FE.ZS?date=2020:2023&format=json&per_page=100",
  "answer_chars": 1122,
  "expected_answer": "Kuwait",
